  "worked_solution": "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=1.$ This means that $k=1$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{a}{x}+1.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(1,3.5)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x}+1 \\\\ 3.5 & =\\frac{a}{1}+1 \\\\ 3.5 & =a+1 \\\\ a & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
